  "methodology": [
    "Fresh local node with instant block driver, pubkey authentication, same pinned Release binaries as timing-profile.json.",
    "Three warmup status transactions per contract, then 30 rounds interleaving Doom, tiny_same_image, tiny_16m, tiny_2m. Each successful transaction produces one block.",
    "All status entrypoints check empty calldata, read an 80-byte metadata item and return it. No Doom simulation, WAD access, snapshot restoration, or game-state writes. Native wallet replay/accounting still applies.",
    "tiny_same_image replaces only the Doom artifact code with a 548-byte control program; initial data and 16 MiB guest size are unchanged. tiny_16m removes unused initial data. tiny_2m additionally lowers guest memory to 2 MiB; its code is identical.",
    "30 direct groundhog_getStorageAt metadata reads after transaction workload and a 50 ms quiescence wait; these do not execute a contract or produce a block.",
    "Transaction totalMs is LiveGame.call time through successful receipt observation, excluding session file save. Raw wallEndNs additionally includes that save; closeToReceiptMs instead uses wallStartNs + totalMs.",
    "Block open/close spans use existing event-service logs at millisecond resolution, not isolated executor CPU time. Medians of separate spans do not add exactly.",
    "This interleaved workload has different allocation/cache behavior and host variance from the earlier 23.45 ms Doom-only status run; do not subtract across separate runs.",
    "Preparation/instantiation microbenchmarks use the separately compiled Zig -O3 harness, 36 repetitions with the first omitted from medians; they are not exact node phase timings.",
    "A first setup attempt hit the previously observed transient DbGateway System error immediately after initialization. This completed run retries setup reads only; measured transactions and quiescent reads all succeeded without retries.",
    "No node source changes or cross-block prepared-code caching changes were made."
  ],
